      "writtenOn": "2016-09-16T21:03:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does randomization really buy us anything?\n\nIt might be more useful to just do reads, writes, and alternating reads/writes in multiple loops to guarantee that whatever metrics we care about are achieved.\n\nMaybe the logic below can be split into helper functions so that reads and writes can invoked deterministically in addition to randomly.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 932,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 932,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "e1a138f29f168ff6a4f93ef7e1bd062984bf5215",
